From: Antigravity Autonomous Agent <engineering@lenovo-d330-fix.local>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/dsi: make the GLK resume enable path take the fresh-probe branch on Lenovo IdeaPad D330

The Lenovo IdeaPad D330-10IGL (82H0) panel stays black after S3 resume, while
unbind/bind (full PCI re-probe) always lights it. Machine evidence
(docs/research/DSI_MMIO_DIFF.md, phase 47) shows the resume enable path and the
working re-probe path differ in exactly one code-visible way: through S3 the
GLK DSI device keeps DEVICE_READY set, so glk_dsi_enable_io() reports
!cold_boot and glk_dsi_device_ready() takes the ULPS enter/exit branch on a
device that was never taken out of ready; the re-probe path starts from
DEVICE_READY=0 and takes the plain re-arm branch.

DMI-gated to 82H0, clear the retained state (ULPS_STATE_MASK + DEVICE_READY,
device off) in intel_dsi_pre_enable() right after the panel VBT power-on and
before the glk_dsi_enable_io() cold-boot probe. The probe then reports fresh
like the re-probe path (cold_boot=1, intel_dsi_prepare() before
intel_dsi_device_ready()), and the existing !(DEVICE_READY) branch re-arms the
device exactly as after a hardware reset.

Sequencing only: the write touches the DEVICE_READY/ULPS on/off state bits, no
operational register values (HS_TX_TIMEOUT, HIGH_LOW_SWITCH_COUNT, ...).

Signed-off-by: Antigravity Autonomous Agent <engineering@lenovo-d330-fix.local>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c | 50 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 50 insertions(+)
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
@@ -717,6 +717,24 @@
  */
 
 /*
+ * Lenovo IdeaPad D330-10IGL (DMI product name 82H0): Gemini Lake DSI panel
+ * machine. The gate is computed once because the DSI enable path is hot and
+ * dmi_match() would otherwise scan the DMI table on every encoder enable.
+ */
+static bool d330_82h0_panel(void)
+{
+	static bool dmi_checked;
+	static bool is_d330_82h0;
+
+	if (!dmi_checked) {
+		is_d330_82h0 = dmi_match(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "82H0");
+		dmi_checked = true;
+	}
+
+	return is_d330_82h0;
+}
+
+/*
  * DSI port enable has to be done before pipe and plane enable, so we do it in
  * the pre_enable hook instead of the enable hook.
  */
@@ -773,6 +791,38 @@
 	msleep(intel_dsi->panel_on_delay);
 	intel_dsi_vbt_exec_sequence(intel_dsi, MIPI_SEQ_DEASSERT_RESET);
 
+	/*
+	 * Lenovo IdeaPad D330-10IGL (82H0): over S3 resume the GLK DSI
+	 * device keeps DEVICE_READY set from the pre-suspend session, while
+	 * the working PCI re-probe path always starts from DEVICE_READY=0
+	 * (hardware reset). The retained state is what makes the resume
+	 * enable path diverge from the reload path: glk_dsi_device_ready()
+	 * then runs the ULPS enter/exit dance on a device that was never
+	 * taken out of ready, and the cold-boot probe below reports
+	 * !cold_boot so intel_dsi_prepare() runs after (not before)
+	 * intel_dsi_device_ready(). When retained state is observed, clear
+	 * it here, before the cold-boot probe, so the whole pre_enable runs
+	 * the same fresh-probe sequence the reload path sees: the probe
+	 * reports DEVICE_READY clear (cold_boot=1, prepare before
+	 * device_ready) and the plain !(DEVICE_READY) branch re-arms it,
+	 * exactly as after a hardware reset.
+	 *
+	 * Sequencing only: ULPS_STATE_MASK and DEVICE_READY are the DSI
+	 * device on/off state bits; no operational register values are
+	 * written.
+	 */
+	if (d330_82h0_panel()) {
+		for_each_dsi_port(port, intel_dsi->ports) {
+			if (intel_de_read(display, MIPI_DEVICE_READY(display, port)) & DEVICE_READY) {
+				drm_info(display->drm,
+					 "[D330 82H0] DSI DEVICE_READY retained, clearing to fresh\n");
+				intel_de_rmw(display, MIPI_DEVICE_READY(display, port),
+					     ULPS_STATE_MASK | DEVICE_READY, 0);
+				usleep_range(10, 15);
+			}
+		}
+	}
+
 	if (display->platform.geminilake) {
 		glk_cold_boot = glk_dsi_enable_io(encoder);
 
